  "body": "If you've been waiting for the right street, a home with personality and the potential to add serious value, this could be the one.\r\n\r\nSet in one of Rothesay Bay's sought-after streets, with the beach at the end of the road and premium homes nearby, this is your chance to secure a coastal address with exciting potential.\r\n\r\nThere's a touch of Hollywood Hills glamour about the arrival, with a substantial brick exterior, tropical palms and unmistakable 1970s flair. Inside, the individuality continues with a striking staircase, a raised ceiling with high-level windows, and sculptural brickwork featuring multiple arched display niches. This is serious retro chic with an identity all its own.\r\n\r\nFour double bedrooms, three bathrooms and two generous living areas provide room for everyone. With three bedrooms upstairs and one downstairs, there's flexibility for multi-generational living, teenagers or adult children wanting their own space. You'll love the spacious master suite, complete with a walk-in wardrobe and ensuite with a separate bath. A true retreat.\r\n\r\nThe outlook is breathtaking, with views towards Rangitoto and the Hauraki Gulf in one direction, and Whangaparaoa and Tiritiri Matangi in the other. From the lounge and kitchen, the scenery becomes part of everyday life, with doors opening onto a covered wraparound deck that extends the living space outdoors. Enjoy a morning coffee with a sunrise view, dine alfresco or head downstairs to the dedicated BBQ zone for relaxed entertaining.\r\n\r\nThere's substantial off-street parking, too, with room for the boat, motorhome and beach toys - a real bonus for coastal living.\r\n\r\nRothesay Bay and Churchill Cove are within walking distance, as is Murrays Bay Wharf, while local cafe's and shops are approximately 300 metres away. Families will appreciate the school zones for Browns Bay Primary, Murrays Bay and Northcross Intermediate and Rangitoto College.\r\n\r\nThe vendor has begun the process to convert to property from cross-lease to freehold. With neighbouring homes demonstrating the appeal of this prestigious street, savvy buyers will recognise the opportunity to secure a premium position and add value now and into the future. \r\n\r\nThe owners are Australia-bound, and this home must be sold!\r\n\r\nAuction: 4:00pm, Wednesday 11 November 2026, In Rooms, Ray White Glenfield, Glenfield Mall (unless sold prior). You can watch the auction live here https://rwcarpenterrealty.co.nz/watch-our-auctions-live",
